**Answer: any two of: general formula; successive members differ by CH₂; similar chemical properties; same functional group.**

A homologous series:

1. can be represented by a **general formula** (e.g. CnH2n for the alkenes);
2. has successive members that **differ by a CH₂ group**;
3. members show **similar chemical properties** (they react in the same way);
4. share the **same functional group**.

Any two of these score the two marks.
